Fifth and last work package of LRT-1 (acceptance gate). Design contract: docs/long-running-tasks.md · Plan: docs/long-running-tasks-plan.md §2 WP4 and §6. Depends on WP1-WP3.

OBJECTIVE
Prove LRT-1 works offline and give management a 5-minute demo they can run without reading code.

SCOPE
1. Offline pytest suite (no network, no LLM, tmp project fixtures):
   - RunLock: exclusivity, stale heartbeat takeover, release;
   - ancestry: spent/budget only counts chats whose root_id is the main task (grandchildren included);
   - budget admission: per-task estimation_cost == min(per_task_budget, remaining - reserve); budget_exhausted triggers at the right number;
   - service transitions: start/pause/resume/stop persisted and reloaded;
   - runner recovery: simulated crash mid-turn -> attempts +1, single worker, no double processing;
   - stagnation: 3 no-progress supervisor turns -> stalled.
2. docs/long-running-tasks-demo.md — one screen, numbered steps with expected result for each:
   (1) POST /api/long-running with a tiny objective -> board + main task appear;
   (2) worker creates 2-3 tasks, the first runs and completes;
   (3) kill the background process mid-run, restart -> run continues with no click;
   (4) pause -> nothing moves; resume -> it moves; stop -> in-flight cancelled;
   (5) force budget_exhausted -> delivery report written without an extra paid turn.

ACCEPTANCE (evidence required in the task report)
- pytest -k run_ green, offline, under 30 seconds (paste the summary line).
- Every demo step has a visible expected result and the commands are copy-pasteable.
- The demo document names the exact endpoints and the board used.

RULES
- Tests must not call a real model, a real socket or the global settings singleton.
- Do not change production behaviour to make a test pass; report the defect instead.

